{
  "task": "Write Python 3 function solve(rows). First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 3 equals 2, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 1 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [start,end] are integer half-open intervals. Discard empty or reversed intervals. Merge overlapping intervals, but do not merge intervals that only touch. Return sorted merged lists.\nReturn the requested value, without printing. Inputs follow the types specified. Do not mutate the input. Standard library is allowed.",
  "specification": "First apply an audit filter to the ORIGINAL input positions, indexed from zero: omit positions whose index modulo 3 equals 2, except always retain the last input position. Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 1 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty). Apply the following rules to that transformed list: Rows [start,end] are integer half-open intervals. Discard empty or reversed intervals. Merge overlapping intervals, but do not merge intervals that only touch. Return sorted merged lists.",
  "reference": "def solve(rows):\n out=[]\n for s,e in sorted(rows):\n  if s>=e: continue\n  if out and s<out[-1][1]: out[-1][1]=max(out[-1][1],e)\n  else: out.append([s,e])\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%3!=2 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=1%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
  "mutation": "def solve(rows):\n out=[]\n for s,e in sorted(rows):\n  if s>=e: continue\n  if out and s<=out[-1][1]: out[-1][1]=max(out[-1][1],e)\n  else: out.append([s,e])\n return out\n_core_solve=solve\ndef solve(rows):\n filtered=[row for i,row in enumerate(rows) if i%3!=2 or i==len(rows)-1]\n if filtered:\n  shift=1%len(filtered)\n  filtered=filtered[shift:]+filtered[:shift]\n return _core_solve(filtered)",
