        "text": "def solve(rows):\n  \"\"\"Applies a series of transformations to a list of rows.\n\n  Args:\n    rows: A list of lists, where each inner list represents a row.\n\n  Returns:\n    A sorted list of merged integer half-open intervals.\n  \"\"\"\n  \n  # Audit filter: Omit positions whose index modulo 3 equals 2, except always retain the last position.\n  filtered_positions = [i for i in range(len(rows)) if i % 3 != 2 or i == len(rows) - 1]\n\n  # Rotate the retained rows LEFT by 1 positions modulo the retained length (empty stays empty).\n  rotated_rows = []\n  for i in range(len(filtered_positions)):\n    start = filtered_positions[i] - (i % len(filtered_positions)) if i > 0 else start\n    end = filtered_positions[i] if i < len(filtered_positions) - 1 else end\n    rotated_rows.append(rows[start:end])\n\n  # Apply rules to that transformed list: Rows [start,end] are integer half-open intervals.\n  # Discard empty or reversed intervals.\n  valid_intervals = []\n  for start, end in rotated_rows:\n    if start < end and start >= 0 and end <= len(rows):\n      valid_intervals.append((start, end))\n\n  # Merge overlapping intervals, but do not merge intervals that only touch.\n  merged_intervals = []\n  valid_intervals.sort()\n  i = 0\n  while i < len(valid_intervals):\n    current_start, current_end = valid_intervals[i]\n    j = i + 1\n    while j < len(valid_intervals) and valid_intervals[j][0] <= current_end + 1:\n      current_end = max(current_end, valid_intervals[j][1])\n      j += 1\n    merged_intervals.append((current_start, current_end))\n    i = j\n\n  # Return sorted merged lists.\n  merged_intervals.sort()\n  return merged_intervals",
